{"id":"8b6d8e45e52b380a","group":"58","path":"58/batch14/58-df-zfc-measure8-convolution-measure.md","title":"ZFC Measure8 Convolution Measure","display":"df-zfc-measure8-convolution-measure — ZFC Measure8 Convolution Measure","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-measure8-convolution-measure","aliases":["58-df-zfc-measure8-convolution-measure"],"display":"df-zfc-measure8-convolution-measure — ZFC Measure8 Convolution Measure","depends_on":["[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","[[../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md]]","[[../batch13/58-df-measure.md]]","[[../batch02/58-df-integral.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-measure8-convolution-measure"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-measure8-convolution-measure</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-measure8-convolution-measure — ZFC Measure8 Convolution Measure"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"a740bdad87b97ac6\" href=\"?note=a740bdad87b97ac6\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md\">../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"ca832ed6bc22f728\" href=\"?note=ca832ed6bc22f728\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-measure.md\">../batch13/58-df-measure.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"4884f45058a56aac\" href=\"?note=4884f45058a56aac\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-integral.md\">../batch02/58-df-integral.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G,m,\\mathcal A,\\mathcal A^{\\otimes2},\\mu,\\nu,\\rho\\in V\">\\(G,m,\\mathcal A,\\mathcal A^{\\otimes2},\\mu,\\nu,\\rho\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}\">\\(\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Measure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Measure}_S\\)</span> are as in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>, <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"a740bdad87b97ac6\" href=\"?note=a740bdad87b97ac6\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md\">../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md</a>, and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"ca832ed6bc22f728\" href=\"?note=ca832ed6bc22f728\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-measure.md\">../batch13/58-df-measure.md</a>.</li>\n<li>The iterated indicator integral is the nonnegative Lebesgue integral of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"4884f45058a56aac\" href=\"?note=4884f45058a56aac\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-integral.md\">../batch02/58-df-integral.md</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ProductSigma}_S\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{ProductSigma}_S\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8ConvolutionMeasure}_S\\subseteq V^7\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8ConvolutionMeasure}_S\\subseteq V^7\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}measure8\\text{-}product\\text{-}sigma}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ProductSigma}_S(\\mathcal A^{\\otimes2},G,\\mathcal A)\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal A^{\\otimes2},G\\times G)\\land\n\\forall A,B\\in\\mathcal A\\;(A\\times B\\in\\mathcal A^{\\otimes2})\\land\n\\forall\\mathcal C\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal C,G\\times G)\\land\n\\forall A,B\\in\\mathcal A\\;(A\\times B\\in\\mathcal C)\n\\to\\mathcal A^{\\otimes2}\\subseteq\\mathcal C\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}measure8\\text{-}product\\text{-}sigma}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ProductSigma}_S(\\mathcal A^{\\otimes2},G,\\mathcal A)\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal A^{\\otimes2},G\\times G)\\land\n\\forall A,B\\in\\mathcal A\\;(A\\times B\\in\\mathcal A^{\\otimes2})\\land\n\\forall\\mathcal C\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal C,G\\times G)\\land\n\\forall A,B\\in\\mathcal A\\;(A\\times B\\in\\mathcal C)\n\\to\\mathcal A^{\\otimes2}\\subseteq\\mathcal C\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}measure8\\text{-}convolution\\text{-}measure} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8ConvolutionMeasure}_S(G,m,\\mathcal A,\\mathcal A^{\\otimes2},\\mu,\\nu,\\rho)\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal A,G)\\land\n\\mathrm{ProductSigma}_S(\\mathcal A^{\\otimes2},G,\\mathcal A)\\land\n\\mathrm{Function}(m,G\\times G,G)\\land\n\\forall x,y,z\\in G\\;m(\\langle m(\\langle x,y\\rangle),z\\rangle)=m(\\langle x,m(\\langle y,z\\rangle)\\rangle)\\land\n\\forall C\\in\\mathcal A\\;\n\\{\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in G\\times G:m(\\langle x,y\\rangle)\\in C\\}\\in\\mathcal A^{\\otimes2}\\land\n\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu,G,\\mathcal A)\\land\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\nu,G,\\mathcal A)\\land\n\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\rho,G,\\mathcal A)\\land\n\\forall C\\in\\mathcal A\\;\\left(\n\\rho(C)=\\int_G\\int_G\\mathbf1_C(m(\\langle x,y\\rangle))\\,d\\mu(x)\\,d\\nu(y)\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}measure8\\text{-}convolution\\text{-}measure} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8ConvolutionMeasure}_S(G,m,\\mathcal A,\\mathcal A^{\\otimes2},\\mu,\\nu,\\rho)\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal A,G)\\land\n\\mathrm{ProductSigma}_S(\\mathcal A^{\\otimes2},G,\\mathcal A)\\land\n\\mathrm{Function}(m,G\\times G,G)\\land\n\\forall x,y,z\\in G\\;m(\\langle m(\\langle x,y\\rangle),z\\rangle)=m(\\langle x,m(\\langle y,z\\rangle)\\rangle)\\land\n\\forall C\\in\\mathcal A\\;\n\\{\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in G\\times G:m(\\langle x,y\\rangle)\\in C\\}\\in\\mathcal A^{\\otimes2}\\land\n\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu,G,\\mathcal A)\\land\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\nu,G,\\mathcal A)\\land\n\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\rho,G,\\mathcal A)\\land\n\\forall C\\in\\mathcal A\\;\\left(\n\\rho(C)=\\int_G\\int_G\\mathbf1_C(m(\\langle x,y\\rangle))\\,d\\mu(x)\\,d\\nu(y)\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Convolution is defined on a measurable semigroup and only on the common sigma algebra; the product sigma algebra, multiplication measurability, and nonnegative-integral source are explicit.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md","status":"resolved","id":"a740bdad87b97ac6","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-measure.md","status":"resolved","id":"ca832ed6bc22f728","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-measure.md]]","embed":false},{"targ